# HTMX

- Fragments are `_name.html` and extend nothing. Full pages extend `base.html`.
- Detect with `apps.common.htmx.is_htmx(request)`, not a raw header string.
- Every trigger has `hx-indicator` and `hx-disabled-elt="this"`.
- Return real status codes and still render a readable fragment; `app.js`
  already enables swapping 400/422/503.
- A direct, non-HTMX hit on a fragment URL must degrade (usually a redirect).
- CSRF comes from `hx-headers` on `<body>`; keep `{% csrf_token %}` in forms.
- Swapped regions announce themselves (`role="status"`, errors `role="alert"`).

See skills: `htmx-patterns`, `django-templates`, `ui-ux`.
